A||||6||Alex2004||First time to drive Fiero on hiway, already have to slam on the brakes ||||11||
Z||000000||Alex2004||06-20-2001||11:06 PM||||I finally got to drive my Fiero on a two lane hiway outside of town, i waited til it was dark so no one could see me ,only have my permit, mom told me i could go and drive it since it needed to be driven since it hasn't been driven in a while, so i went to the rodeo grounds (dirt road) and drove around for a few and then went on the hiway, it's basically just a 2 lane road, speed limit is 65, and was just coming out of the curve doing about 55 and a cyotee (or however you spell it), i had to slame on my brakes, they didn't lock up though, but i never realized how hard it is to stop doing 55. That really freaked me out, i'm just glad i didnt hit it.  But now my temp gauge works! LOL, so i'm happy that is fixed, i replaced it and i guess i never got it hot enough to show... Just thought i'd tell you guys and girls since it was my frist time to actaully DRIVE it on the hiway and my first close call...<P>Alex...  <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||11
